# Cursor Project Rules

## Writing and Style
- Do not use emojis.
- Do not use emdashes.

## File and Directory Discipline
- Always investigate before creating or modifying files. The SHADE-Arena repo is in the project for you to explore only and mimic their approach where possible.
- Before creating a new file or directory, check if a similar one already exists, to avoid duplication and maintain consistent structure across the project.
- Do not create .md or test files unless asked to.

## Workflow Expectations
- Before making any change, review the README and follow all instructions and conventions described there.
- When uncertain, prefer inspecting the existing codebase, structure, and naming patterns before generating new content.

## General Behavior
- Prioritize consistency with the current project structure.
- Preserve existing patterns, style, and architecture.
- Do not run test files.